d its maximum capacity is $88$ computers. Let $C(t)$ be the number of computers, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in months. Its population obeys an inhibited growth model. The rate of increase equals $\\frac{1}{3}$ times the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Which differential equation models this population?" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537154 1072 #uuid "3f5ed13c-38a0-569e-996e-43867fd33621" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537154 1074 "The rate at which the number of computers $C(t)$ in the data center changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current number of computers. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-C),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=88$ computers, and $k=\\frac{1}{3}$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{3}(88-C).\n$$" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537155 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{461}{3}-N" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537155 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537155 1083 #uuid "3ffd4e28-fda9-566f-ad4b-4df3672f98dc" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537156 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=2(44-N)" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537156 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537156 1083 #uuid "41f9afda-dab8-5ea1-a543-78cd7ef01897" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537157 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=2(88-C)" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537157 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537157 1083 #uuid "4bd1d390-d8de-540e-9210-b415fa61cff9" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537158 1080 "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=5(452-B)" 13194139535891 17592186045443 true] [17592186537158 1082 #edb/re